From: nim-gtk2 native persistence regression
Subject: [PATCH] clipboard: retain store timeout until store's existing cleanup removes it

GTK 2.24.33's store-timeout callback quits the loop and returns FALSE, removing
its own source. gtk_clipboard_store then unconditionally calls g_source_remove
on the expired ID. Modern GLib reports a critical (fatal under G_DEBUG=fatal-warnings).

Keep the timeout registered until the existing synchronous store cleanup removes
it after the loop unwinds. This does not change the native deadline, return type,
manager acceptance semantics or ownership. No second timeout/claim is fabricated.

Optional GTK SOURCE patch only. The SDK does not apply it, suppress the warning,
mutate private timer fields or change installed libraries. Rebuild GTK separately.
Diagnostic: isolated DISPLAY, GTK2_TEST_VIRTUAL_DISPLAY=1, G_DEBUG=fatal-warnings,
  nimble probeNativeClipboardStoreTimeout
The unpatched native regression exits 1; a separately rebuilt patched library must
be validated independently. A normal return still does not prove storage success.

--- a/gtk/gtkclipboard.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkclipboard.c
@@ -1923,7 +1923,8 @@
 {
   g_main_loop_quit (clipboard->store_loop);
   
-  return FALSE;
+  /* gtk_clipboard_store removes this source after the loop unwinds. */
+  return TRUE;
 }
 
